From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:59:09 +0000
Subject: net: r8169: skip the HW tally counter dump on RTL8127A

On CIX Sky1 boards with the on-board RTL8127A (MAC_VER_80), any MMIO
access to the NIC BAR from the stats path faults once the device has
powered down its BAR, and escalates to a fatal ARM SError (first
observed via systemd-resolved's RTNL poll ~10 s after boot: the
CounterDump DMA faults, then the ChipCmd read itself, ESR 0xbe000011).
The same access pattern panics the shutdown path when the tally dump
runs from rtl_shutdown. The NIC reports pm_runtime "active" while its
BAR is actually inaccessible.

Bail out of rtl8169_update_counters() before touching any register on
RTL8127A; get_stats64 falls back to the software counters.

Validated on Radxa Orion O6 metal: no more SError on the RTNL stats
poll and clean reboots with the RTL8127A NIC.
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
index 791277e75..d8b646b02 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/realtek/r8169_main.c
@@ -1932,7 +1932,21 @@ static void rtl8169_do_counters(struct rtl8169_private *tp, u32 counter_cmd)
 
 static void rtl8169_update_counters(struct rtl8169_private *tp)
 {
-	u8 val = RTL_R8(tp, ChipCmd);
+	u8 val;
+
+	/*
+	 * CIX Sky1: on the RTL8127A (MAC_VER_80) any MMIO to the NIC BAR from
+	 * the stats path faults once the device has powered down its BAR, and
+	 * escalates to a fatal ARM SError (seen via systemd-resolved's RTNL
+	 * poll ~10 s after boot: first the CounterDump DMA, then the ChipCmd
+	 * read itself, ESR 0xbe000011). The NIC reports pm_runtime "active"
+	 * while its BAR is actually inaccessible. Bail out before touching
+	 * any register -- @get_stats64 returns the software counters.
+	 */
+	if (tp->mac_version >= RTL_GIGA_MAC_VER_80)
+		return;
+
+	val = RTL_R8(tp, ChipCmd);
 
 	/*
 	 * Some chips are unable to dump tally counters when the receiver
